Hello!

I was wondering if it would be a valid aproach to perform a model test (e.g. AICc) comparing the likelihood values of a time-stratified analysis (+dispersal multipliers differing among time slices) with a non-time stritified, no dispersal multipliers analysis.

The dispersal multipliers seems to count as model parameters (when w=1 - although i'm not sure of this interpretation either), but the time slices that i can impose to the tree seems to affect the data, which would not allow this aproach. Is this it?

Best

